	[[ This one seems to have got lost along the way...]]

	[Remember those pictures that used to come out on the lineprinter
	 late at night?  Here's a collection of lineprinter art.  I have
	 compressed and uuencode the originals for three reasons:
	 1) a lot of duplicated characters, reaps great benefits by
	 compression, 2) all of the lines are 132 characters long, which
	 render them susceptable to truncation by BITNET nodes, and 3) many
	 lines have trailing spaces, which render them susceptable to munging
	 by BITNET nodes.  When you uudecode and uncompress the files you
	 get "real source" - so no flak please.   -br
	 P.S. I used to have a whole tape of these kinds of things, but
	 they got lost along the way.  Anyone else have agood collection
	 they'd like to contribute?]

#! /bin/sh
# This is a shell archive.  Remove anything before this line, then unpack
# it by saving it into a file and typing "sh file".  To overwrite existing
# files, type "sh file -c".  You can also feed this as standard input via
# unshar, or by typing "sh <file", e.g..  If this archive is complete, you
# will see the following message at the end:
#		"End of archive 1 (of 3)."
# Contents:  README MANIFEST christus.Z.uu ffilter.c freudleft.Z.uu
#   horse.Z.uu kapel.Z.uu venus.Z.uu
# Wrapped by billr@saab on Mon Mar 13 15:03:05 1989
PATH=/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/ucb ; export PATH
if test -f 'README' -a "${1}" != "-c" ; then 
  echo shar: Will not clobber existing file \"'README'\"
else
echo shar: Extracting \"'README'\" \(813 characters\)
sed "s/^X//" >'README' <<'END_OF_FILE'
XThis is a set of pictures suitable for printing on a line printer.
Xuudecode and uncompress the files then feed them to your line printer.
XNote that the print files are formatted with ASA (ANSI) carriage
Xcontrol characters in column 1.  A '1' means new page, a ' ' means
Xprint text on next line and '+' means overprint this line on the
Xprevious one.
X
XThe Berkeley line printer spooler supplies a switch for a filter to
Xconvert this format to whatever your printer requires (-f).  Unfortun-
Xately, they don't supply the filter itself.
X
XI wrote a simple filter to work with one of our printers (ffilter.c).
XFrom looking at the manuals for our Printronix P600, though, I don't
Xsee any way to write a filter that will work for it.
X
X	-Bill Randle
X	Moderator, comp.sources.games
X	Tektronix, Inc.
X	billr@saab.CNA.TEK.COM
END_OF_FILE
